      "row_0": "min_y",
      "source": "shared/world/out/farfield_height.png, decoded by shared.terrain.heightmap.load_far_field"
    }
  },
  "far_field_note": "The far field is vertex-for-vertex with the block at its edge and carries the block's own heights inside it, so a 3D scene can draw it past the edge as a ring and leave the block's own terrain to cover the middle. The ridge ring, the river's valley reaches and the northern skyline stand on it.",
  "heightmap_note": "heightmap.png is 16-bit grayscale; a browser cannot read its sample values back, which is the only reason hillshade.png and the two .f32 grids exist at all. The 2D viewer never decodes it; the 3D scene reads heightmap.f32 instead."
